{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>וישב, אונם</b> — like ועולתה קפצה פיה (from the root עול, 'iniquity' — cf. און): what they plotted to do to me, HaShem brought upon them." "<b>וטעם יצמיתם</b> — sometimes the evil they plotted to do to me is what destroys [מצמית] them, and sometimes HaShem destroys them in another way, that did not cross their minds."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra draws a grammatical parallel between אונם and עולתה, both from the root ע-ו-ל/א-ו-ן; the parenthetical clarification is implicit in his compressed comparison."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:19.379941738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}